{"author":{"id":"0fb62b7075a4219f84b4bf8c9c235af1632f3fa4b63ca899f025ad8215a930fd"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778070874,"nonce":"CyTKTl/B/RN8hU//IXC2KO6I43w=","title":"data/masters.RDS carries no embedded provenance — no snapshot date, no source-repository identifier, no list of institutions covered, no version of the processing script that produced it. A consumer reading the file alone cannot answer \"when was this collected, what code produced it, what is included\".","message":"- Write a sidecar data/masters_metadata.json (or .yaml) at the end of data-raw/masters.R, capturing:\n  - snapshot_date (raw export date — e.g. 2025-03 from filenames)\n  - generated_at (timestamp of the run)\n  - git_sha (HEAD at run time)\n  - source: \"Brage local repositories\"\n  - institutions: list with row counts per institution\n  - schema_version (bump when columns/semantics change)\n  - notes / known issues (link to README sections)\n- Optionally also `attr(masters, \"metadata\") \u003c- ...` so it travels with the RDS.\n- If the portable-export bug ships CSV/Parquet, the same metadata should accompany those files.\n\nIndependent of the data-dictionary bug (dictionary describes columns; metadata describes the snapshot), but they're natural partners in the open-release workflow. Should also wait until the Oslomet GFU_2024 fix lands so the recorded row counts are correct.","files":null}]}